  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 5.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "erm, morning, doctor lovely to meet you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.59,
      "end_seconds": 10.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.28,
      "end_seconds": 15.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.27,
      "end_seconds": 19.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "please do extra information is always welcome"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.23,
      "end_seconds": 25.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Yeah, it's bloating after meals. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.19,
      "end_seconds": 30.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.03,
      "end_seconds": 35.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I'd say about a month, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 37.24,
      "end_seconds": 41.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "uh, it was closer to about two months, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.2,
      "end_seconds": 50.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.12,
      "end_seconds": 59.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Yes, you know, somewhere around that. I've also had loose stools now and then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.67,
      "end_seconds": 62.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "have you noticed any triggers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.64,
      "end_seconds": 71.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "It's, It's worse with stress. I've also had a lot of wind, for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.05,
      "end_seconds": 74.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.48,
      "end_seconds": 77.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.55,
      "end_seconds": 84.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Have you had any night-time diarrhoea, blood in the stool or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.64,
      "end_seconds": 90.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Yeah, um, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.57,
      "end_seconds": 94.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Have you had vomiting, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.49,
      "end_seconds": 97.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Definitely no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 97.68,
      "end_seconds": 102.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.31,
      "end_seconds": 109.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.29,
      "end_seconds": 120.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.43,
      "end_seconds": 122.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "nothing odd there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.47,
      "end_seconds": 142.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.18,
      "end_seconds": 147.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.27,
      "end_seconds": 152.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 153.53,
      "end_seconds": 173.06,
      "duration_seconds": 19.53,
      "text": "She takes escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. She is on iron tablets, once a day for my blood count, I give it to her. Um, it's metoprolol, twice a day for my heart, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.86,
      "end_seconds": 177.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 178.35,
      "end_seconds": 179.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "It's 50 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.89,
      "end_seconds": 183.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 185.74,
      "end_seconds": 193.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "for about a month. She is on peppermint capsules, after meals, I give it to her"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.95,
      "end_seconds": 199.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "so, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.06,
      "end_seconds": 203.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I've, I've had anxiety, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.04,
      "end_seconds": 205.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.38,
      "end_seconds": 210.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Low haemoglobin, for about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.42,
      "end_seconds": 213.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.73,
      "end_seconds": 218.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "okay, so I've had an underactive thyroid, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.08,
      "end_seconds": 221.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.9,
      "end_seconds": 225.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I've had heart failure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.91,
      "end_seconds": 233.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Alright, anxiety and an underactive thyroid, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.0,
      "end_seconds": 252.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.97,
      "end_seconds": 269.32,
      "duration_seconds": 16.35,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I have about eight cigarettes in a day. I retired from the post office two years ago. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.55,
      "end_seconds": 279.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.75,
      "end_seconds": 284.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "my mother has an underactive thyroid"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 286.58,
      "end_seconds": 294.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 86, temp 36.8 degrees, blood pressure 124 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.99,
      "end_seconds": 297.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.98,
      "end_seconds": 304.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Right, now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.57,
      "end_seconds": 307.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.42,
      "end_seconds": 327.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft and not tender, and and I can't feel any lumps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.46,
      "end_seconds": 351.36,
      "duration_seconds": 19.9,
      "text": "Alright, thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? It It points towards a functional bowel pattern, with no alarm features. Another possibility is irritable bowel syndrome. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had bloating after meals, and no night-time diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.59,
      "end_seconds": 353.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "correct"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.42,
      "end_seconds": 392.07,
      "duration_seconds": 25.65,
      "text": "I think a coeliac blood test makes sense here, for bloating. Try smaller meals and keep a a food and symptom diary for four weeks. If you see blood in the stool or lose weight, that's the point to come in urgently. Book a review in six weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.12,
      "end_seconds": 395.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}